+//! Consistency-checker **workload + serializer** slice (issue #406, ADR-0041 decision 1–3,
+//! #329 slice 3): the load-bearing, `cargo xtask ci`-run regression for the machinery built
+//! on top of the merged #405 networked observable
+//! ([`wyrd_server::consistency_observable`]). It carries BOTH halves the brief names:
+//!
+//! * the **socket-free crafted-history reds** — a genuine, flippable, module-weakening
+//!   red→green on real inputs, producible even where the Check sandbox denies loopback
+//!   `bind`: the Elle-EDN serializer's **byte-exact golden** (register + directory-as-set,
+//!   including the indeterminate `:info` mappings), the session read-your-writes (incl. the
+//!   delete-then-read case) / monotonic-read rejections, the reused per-key monotonicity
+//!   rejection, the concurrency witness that requires a read↔write overlap, and the
+//!   verdict-dispatch routing; and
+//! * the **wire-driven concurrent-workload** non-vacuity / concurrency witnesses — ≥2
+//!   concurrent `ObservableS3Client`s over the real in-process S3 HTTP wire producing a
+//!   genuinely concurrent (read↔write-overlapping), version-climbing, monotone-read
+//!   multi-process history (green confirmed by the full `cargo xtask ci`, which permits
+//!   loopback bind).
+//!
+//! The linearizability **verdict** itself is Elle's (JVM/Clojure), and per ADR-0041/ADR-0016
+//! runs **only off-Check** over the SAME serialized history — [`verdict_dispatch`] is the
+//! seam that routes it there; this in-gate slice does NOT return a register/namespace
+//! linearizability verdict.
+//!
+//! RED before the workload/serializer/session-check/directory/verdict machinery exists (the
+//! `consistency_workload` module is absent, so nothing to construct); GREEN once it does, and
+//! it STAYS red whenever the serializer / a session check / the concurrency witness / the
+//! dispatch is weakened.
+
+use std::net::SocketAddr;
+use std::sync::Arc;
+use std::time::{Duration, SystemTime, UNIX_EPOCH};
+
+use tokio::net::TcpListener;
+use wyrd_chunkstore_fs::FsChunkStore;
+use wyrd_coordination_mem::MemCoordination;
+use wyrd_gateway_s3::sigv4::Credentials;
+use wyrd_gateway_s3::{S3Config, S3Gateway};
+use wyrd_metadata_redb::RedbMetadataStore;
+use wyrd_server::consistency_observable::{History, OpKind, OpRecord};
+use wyrd_server::consistency_workload::{
